  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzdotrufck2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "When you think about the Labs' weird approach to software releases (sudden changes, bad communication), it is worth remembering that a core belief is that these products are a temporary thing they have to do to raise money for a couple years until \"true\" AGI makes all products obsolete.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzdotrufck2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T15:57:21.227Z",
      "likes": 50,
      "replies": 4,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 6.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 3.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:eqgbahkj5art5neligzjeqs7/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzazk5zyhc2b",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "AI resistant learning conditions are just less exploitative teacher worker conditions.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzazk5zyhc2b",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-01T14:30:50.389Z",
      "likes": 44,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 8,
      "score": 6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.8,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 28.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mz7swluwac2w",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The Pro series of GPT models continues to be really impressive for one-shot problems that involve complex calculations, references, or sophisticated ideas.\n\nIt isn't particularly fast (or particularly pleasant) to use but GPT-6 Astra Pro gives that \"ask one question of the great oracle\" feel.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mz7swluwac2w",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-01T02:59:51.629Z",
      "likes": 62,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 2,
      "score": 6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.9,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 40.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzdovahtuk2l",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The thing is that their products are unreasonably effective & getting better all the time because LLMs are unreasonably effective & getting better all the time. So the Labs have been rewarded for treating their products as disposable because conventional software cycles broke.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mzdovahtuk2l",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T15:58:10.099Z",
      "likes": 27,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 5.9,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.5,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 3.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mzbzsaina22v",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Music is social. Knowing the same songs is a way that in-groups and out-groups form. AI music is fundamentally anti-social.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mzbzsaina22v",
      "posted_at": "2026-11-02T00:08:01.142Z",
      "likes": 17,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.5,
      "score_parts": {
